ion] A 10-second stylized dance video shows <Subject 1> performing a fast yet elegant classical Chinese dance in a misty forest formed in the graphite line-art style of <Subject 2>. <Subject 1>'s identity, long black hair, pale-blue embroidered costume, translucent sleeves, and flowing skirt are preserved from <Picture 1>, while the monochrome pencil rendering, expressive gesture lines, loose contours, and white-space composition are transferred from <Picture 2>. The motion should feel continuous, lively, graceful, and clearly choreographed rather than random.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout the entire video): fully_preserved - retain the woman's facial identity, long dark hair, pale-blue classical Chinese costume, translucent sleeves, floral embroidery, long skirt, jewelry, and elegant proportions from <Picture 1>. The costume may stretch and flutter naturally during movement, but its color and structural design remain recognizable.\n<Subject 2> (applies throughout the entire video): style_transfer - transfer the black-and-white graphite sketch appearance, expressive pencil contours, loose gestural strokes, directional motion marks, delicate hatching, and white negative space from <Picture 2> to the woman, forest, lighting, and camera image.\n<Subject 3> (appears throughout the entire video): newly_created - create a sparse misty woodland in the transferred graphite sketch style, serving as a quiet, airy background that does not compete with the dancer.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe entire 10-second video is rendered as a refined animated graphite drawing with monochrome black, soft gray, and white values. Keep <Subject 1> recognizable from <Picture 1>, but reinterpret her appearance through the loose, expressive hand-drawn line quality of <Picture 2>. The pale-blue costume is represented with very light cool-gray graphite shading and a subtle restrained blue-gray tint, while the floral embroidery remains visible through fine pencil details. Avoid photorealism, glossy 3D rendering, anime cel shading, or a fully colored realistic look.\n\n[Shot 1: 00:00-00:02.000]\nA wide vertical composition establishes <Subject 3>, a sparse misty forest with tall thin trunks, drifting mist, lightly suggested leaves, and a mostly white background. <Subject 1> stands slightly right of center in a three-quarter view. Her long black hair and translucent sleeves are lifted by the breeze. She begins with a poised classical Chinese dance stance: one foot grounded, the other stepping lightly forward, one arm curved above her head and the other extended diagonally outward. The camera makes a subtle forward push-in. Loose graphite motion lines around her sleeves and hair establish the energetic hand-drawn style.\n\n[Shot 2: 00:02.000-00:04.500]\nThe camera shifts into a medium full-body tracking shot as <Subject 1> accelerates into a fast sequence of classical Chinese dance steps. She performs two light traveling steps through the forest, pivots smoothly, then makes a controlled half-turn. Her long skirt arcs outward in a clean circular sweep, and the translucent sleeves trail behind her arms. Her upper body remains graceful and upright while her footwork is quick and precise. Use expressive curved pencil strokes to emphasize the direction of her spin, fabric movement, and flowing hair. Keep her face, hairstyle, costume silhouette, and body proportions stable across frames.\n\n[Shot 3: 00:04.500-00:07.000]\nIn a fluid continuation, <Subject 1> performs a rapid diagonal leap toward the left side of the frame, landing softly and immediately transitioning into a low turning step. Her arms open like unfolding ribbons, then cross briefly in front of her torso before extending outward again. The forest trunks slide gently in parallax behind her. The graphite animation should show subtle successive sketch traces around her hands, feet, hair, and sleeves, suggesting speed without creating confusing duplicate limbs. Her movement is beautiful, disciplined, and expressive, inspired by classical Chinese dance rather than martial arts.\n\n[Shot 4: 00:07.000-00:09.000]\nThe camera arcs around <Subject 1> in a smooth semicircle from front three-quarter view to side view. She executes a fast elegant spin with one leg extended low and the skirt flaring in a broad crescent. Her head turns slightly after the body, creating a graceful delayed follow-through. Fine pencil hatching defines the folds of the dress, while energetic loose contour lines accent the sleeve tips and hair strands. The mist and tree branches remain soft and sparse, preserving generous white negative space.\n\n[Shot 5: 00:09.000-00:10.000]\nThe movement resolves into a final classical Chinese dance pose. <Subject 1> finishes facing slightly toward the camera, one arm extended upward and the other curved near her waist, with one foot pointed lightly behind her. Her hair and sleeves continue to settle for a moment after the final turn. The camera ends on a medium full-body frame with a subtle push-in. The last image is a clean, elegant graphite illustration with a few lingering pencil motion lines fading into the white mist. End without a hard cut, morphing, facial distortion, extra limbs, or loss of costume details.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft misty woodland ambience with gentle leaf rustling, light wind moving through thin branches, subtle fabric movement from the dancer's sleeves and skirt, and delicate footfalls on damp forest ground. The soundscape remains restrained and airy, allowing the visual pencil movement to remain the focus.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA fast but elegant instrumental score inspired by classical Chinese dance, led by light bamboo flute, plucked guzheng, delicate xiao flute phrases, and restrained hand percussion. The tempo is lively enough to support rapid footwork, approximately 125-135 BPM, while maintaining a graceful poetic feeling. Begin softly, build energy during the traveling steps and spins, then resolve with a brief sustained flute note during the final pose. No vocals, no modern electronic beat, and no dramatic cinematic impact."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#3f5159", "size": [683.4913330078125, 442.0965881347656], "pos": [-105.74380493164062, 5551.28564453125], "id": 232, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.36.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"value": true}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 9}, {"outputs": [{"name": "VIDEO", "links": [], "label": "VIDEO", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "VIDEO"}], "color": "#223", "widgets_values": [24, 8, "sRGB", "none"], "inputs": [{"name": "images", "link": 428, "label": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "images"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "audio", "link": 429, "label": "audio", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "audio"}, {"widget": {"name": "fps"}, "name": "fps", "label": "fps", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "fps"}, {"widget": {"name": "bit_depth"}, "shape": 7, "name": "bit_depth", "label": "bit_depth", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "bit_depth"}, {"widget": {"name": "color_space"}, "shape": 7, "name": "color_space", "label": "color_space", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "color_space"}, {"widget": {"name": "codec"}, "shape": 7, "name": "codec", "label": "codec", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "codec"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CreateVideo", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#335", "size": [218.5041046142578, 150], "pos": [645.4741821289062, 5115.47265625], "id": 234, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.36.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"fps": true, "bit_depth": true}, "Node name for S&R": "CreateVideo", "ttNbgOv